# SINGLE-OWNER SUB-PLACE — the OTHER remedy is not available, and that is
# RATIFIED, not a gap. `^h.f` is `E_PartialMove`: D10(a) ADDENDUM
# (decisions.md, 2026-09-02) rejects field/index moves — no holes, no unpack.
# So at a sub-place `.clone()` is the ONLY in-language remedy, which is exactly
# what the widened diagnostic prescribes.
#
# This cell is what stops the accept-control cell from being read as "either
# `^` or `.clone()` works here": one of the two is a different rejection, and a
# reader who assumes otherwise writes `^h.f` and gets a diagnostic that looks
# like the gate misfiring.
#
# CELL: type=Callable · place=field of a local · position=bind · sigil=`^`.
# Pre-existing behaviour (NOT introduced by this track): rc 1 at 7bf11017e too,
# with `E_PartialMove`. It pins the REMEDY CONTRACT, not a new reject.

struct Holder:
    Callable[int()] f

Callable[int()] mk(int n):
    return (): n + 1

void main():
    Holder h = Holder(mk(40))
    Callable[int()] g = ^h.f
    print(g())
